{
  "name": "Resilience demo: retry, continue on fail, error output, error workflow, sub-workflow",
  "meta": {
    "description": "Three linked workflows that show how FlowForge handles failures: retry on fail, continue on fail, a red error output, a Stop and Error that starts a separate Error Trigger workflow, and a sub-workflow called with Execute Workflow. Imported together.",
    "categories": [
      "Utilities",
      "Webhooks"
    ]
  },
  "workflows": [
    {
      "key": "main",
      "name": "Resilience demo",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "manual",
          "name": "Run by hand",
          "type": "flowforge.manualTrigger",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            -120
          ],
          "parameters": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "hook",
          "name": "Call from outside",
          "type": "flowforge.webhook",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            100
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "httpMethod": "POST",
            "path": "resilience-demo",
            "responseMode": "onReceived"
          },
          "webhookId": "resilience-example"
        },
        {
          "id": "orders",
          "name": "Orders",
          "type": "flowforge.code",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            280,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "jsCode": "// POST {\"crash\": true} to make the whole run fail at the end (the error workflow then runs).\nconst crash = $input.first()?.json?.body?.crash === true;\nreturn [\n  { id: 1, qty: 2, price: 10, country: 'FR' },\n  { id: 2, qty: -1, price: 25, country: 'FR' },\n  { id: 3, qty: 5, price: 4, country: 'XX' },\n].map(o => ({ ...o, crash }));"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "validate",
          "name": "Validate order",
          "type": "flowforge.code",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            560,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
            "jsCodeEachItem": "if ($json.qty < 0) throw new Error('Order ' + $json.id + ' has a negative quantity');\nreturn { ...$json, valid: true };"
          },
          "retryOnFail": true,
          "maxTries": 2,
          "waitBetweenTries": 0,
          "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
          "notes": "Retry on fail (2 tries), then the failing item leaves by the red error output."
        },
        {
          "id": "problem",
          "name": "Report invalid order",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            840,
            200
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "mode": "manual",
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "name": "alert",
                  "value": "=Skipped: {{ $json.error }}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "sub",
          "name": "Calculate price (sub-workflow)",
          "type": "flowforge.executeWorkflow",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            840,
            -100
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "source": "database",
            "workflowId": "ref:sub",
            "mode": "once"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tax",
          "name": "Look up tax rate",
          "type": "flowforge.code",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            1120,
            -100
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
            "jsCodeEachItem": "if ($json.country === 'XX') throw new Error('No tax rate for country ' + $json.country);\nreturn { ...$json, tax: Math.round($json.total * 0.2 * 100) / 100 };"
          },
          "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
          "notes": "Continue on fail: the item goes on with an error field instead of stopping the run."
        },
        {
          "id": "crash",
          "name": "Crash requested?",
          "type": "flowforge.if",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            1400,
            -100
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "conditions": {
              "conditions": [
                {
                  "leftValue": "={{ $json.crash }}",
                  "rightValue": "",
                  "operator": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "operation": "true",
                    "singleValue": true
                  }
                }
              ],
              "combinator": "and"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "stop",
          "name": "Stop and Error",
          "type": "flowforge.stopAndError",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            1680,
            -200
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "errorType": "errorMessage",
            "errorMessage": "Crash requested by the caller (resilience demo)"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "done",
          "name": "All good",
          "type": "flowforge.noOp",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            1680,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "note",
          "name": "How to use",
          "type": "flowforge.stickyNote",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            -40,
            -420
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "content": "## Resilience demo (3 workflows)\n**Run it by hand**: Execute workflow. Order 2 fails validation and leaves by the error output; order 3 fails the tax lookup but continues with an error field; the sub-workflow computes the totals.\n**See the error workflow**: Activate, then `curl -X POST <Production URL> -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"crash\":true}'`. The run fails on purpose and the workflow **Resilience: error handler** starts and writes `data/files/flowforge-demo/errors.log`.\nImport created all three workflows together."
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "Run by hand": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Orders",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Call from outside": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Orders",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Orders": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Validate order",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Validate order": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Calculate price (sub-workflow)",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "node": "Report invalid order",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Calculate price (sub-workflow)": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Look up tax rate",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Look up tax rate": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Crash requested?",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Crash requested?": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Stop and Error",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "node": "All good",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "errorWorkflow": "ref:error"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "sub",
      "name": "Resilience: calculate price (sub-workflow)",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "t",
          "name": "When executed by another workflow",
          "type": "flowforge.executeWorkflowTrigger",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "calc",
          "name": "Compute total",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            280,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "mode": "manual",
            "includeOtherFields": true,
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "name": "total",
                  "value": "={{ $json.qty * $json.price }}",
                  "type": "number"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "When executed by another workflow": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Compute total",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "error",
      "name": "Resilience: error handler",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "e",
          "name": "Error Trigger",
          "type": "flowforge.errorTrigger",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "msg",
          "name": "Build alert",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            280,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "mode": "manual",
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "name": "log",
                  "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}  {{ $json.workflow.name }} failed at \"{{ $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted }}\": {{ $json.execution.error.message }}\\n",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "file",
          "name": "Log to text file",
          "type": "flowforge.convertToFile",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            560,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "operation": "text",
            "sourceProperty": "log",
            "binaryPropertyName": "data",
            "options": {
              "fileName": "errors.log"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "w",
          "name": "Append to errors.log",
          "type": "flowforge.readWriteFile",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            840,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "operation": "write",
            "fileName": "flowforge-demo/errors.log",
            "dataPropertyName": "data",
            "options": {
              "append": true
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "Error Trigger": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Build alert",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Build alert": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Log to text file",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Log to text file": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Append to errors.log",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
